abstract: >-
  Lean 4 proof of finite realizer rank rigidity: for every two-order realizer
  of an occupied-grid sample, one global axis exchange gives both interior
  rank error bounds of at most 30rn under explicit marginal and boundary
  hypotheses. The accompanying draft derives the restricted density inverse
  bound d_conf <= 100 (N^(-1/12) + Delta_N) in prose. Only the deterministic
  finite theorem is Lean verified. Novelty and independent review remain
  unconfirmed. Software is Apache-2.0; the manuscript is CC-BY-4.0.
